    gas_electric_power_monthly_level: { cell: "I", ev: "INERT, MEASURED AT ZERO LP COST (caiso-fuelvintage-1, 2026-09-09; probe scripts/probes/_caiso_fuelvintage_ep_identity.py, results/calibration/_caiso_fuelvintage_ep_identity{,_2425}.json; FINDING-caiso-fuelvintage-1-2026-09-09.md §2). The pre-registration (FINDING-xiso-fuelvintage §5b) predicted NEAR-inert by ordering; the measurement is EXACTLY inert, and no LP was spent to establish it (rule 29 [R-SCREEN] clause (0): an arm with a computable pre-solve gate does not reach a solve until that gate passes). TWO INDEPENDENT LEGS. (1) COVERAGE, 2019-2021: iso_electric_power_monthly_level('CAISO', y) returns None for y in 2019, 2020, 2021 — California prints only 11 of 12 N3045 months in each, so the admission test refuses the year and the caller is byte-identical by construction. (2) ORDERING, 2022-2025 (all four ADMIT, 12/12 months, annual 9.486 / 7.033 / 3.606 / 4.275 $/MMBtu, reconciling the phase-0 table to ~0.04): two fleet_only rebuilds per year on the keeper caiso260_demand_vintage's own recipe, seam off vs on, give max |delta fuel_prices| = 0.000000 and max |delta mc_base| = 0.000000 in EVERY year, with 0 of ~1,710 unit rows moved and a moved gas-cell share of 0.000000. The cause is the keeper's own gas_hub_basis_overlay, which the solve log measures repricing 1,491 / 1,496 / 1,501 gas generators at the measured hub spot in 12/12 months of 2022 / 2024 / 2025 — the more local measured marginal series, which supersedes a state average by construction (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]). THE ONE PLACE THE SEAM DOES WRITE, and why it still cannot reach the LP: the ISO-level _gas_series (which keys ONLY the coal passthrough sigmoid) moves in 2025 by up to 0.535 $/MMBtu, confined to Sep/Oct/Nov — the same three months the gas_hub_basis_overlay cell records as 9/12 ISO-level coverage (caiso-242). It reaches nothing: CAISO carries no coal, and mc_base is measured bit-identical in 2025 regardless. The prompt's premise that the overlay covers 12/12 at BOTH layers is therefore false at the ISO layer and true at the plant layer, which is the layer the LP reads. Dec-2022 — the pre-registered +16.058 $/MMBtu (~120 $/MWh) western-gas-crisis month, CAISO's one materially reachable ISO-month — is INERT for the same reason and is the sharpest case: the seam is superseded exactly where it would have bitten hardest. DO-NOT-REDO for CAISO without new evidence; the mechanism is not refuted, it is unreachable behind a strictly better measured series. A CAISO arm becomes meaningful only if the hub overlay is disarmed or its plant-layer coverage falls below 12/12. || SOLVE-LEVEL CONFIRMATION AND PROMOTION (caiso-fuelvintage-1, 2026-09-09): the arm was SOLVED with the flag armed over 2023-2025 in one invocation plus the 2022 validation touchpoint, and PROMOTED TO KEEPER (2026-09-09-caiso-fuelvintage-860-gas, bundle caiso_fuelvintage_span, DETERMINATION CALIBRATED) on the owner ruling of 2026-09-09 (handoff xiso-fuelvintage SSA7: 'these should be promoted as keepers on both 860 and gas shape counts regardless of inertness'). The cell stays I: inertness is confirmed in DISPATCH, not merely in the offer arrays - the keeper's criterion statuses are unchanged from the superseded caiso-260 (C1/C2/C3a/C3b/C4/C6/C8 PASS, C3c the single ledgered caveat). Promotion is therefore a PROVENANCE act, not a performance claim: CAISO now carries the measured monthly LEVEL as a declared input even though the hub overlay supersedes it everywhere. DO-NOT-REDO stands unchanged - a CAISO arm becomes meaningful only if gas_hub_basis_overlay is disarmed or its plant-layer coverage falls below 12/12. RESULT-caiso-fuelvintage-2026-09-09.md sec 2." },
